response:
Sure!  Do loops and while loops are two types of loops that allow a program to repeat a section of code multiple times.  The "do" loop is used when you know how many times the code will run, like this:

for (int i=0; i<10; i++) {
    doSomething();
}

The "while" loop is used when you don’t know how many times the code will run, like this:

int i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
    doSomething();
    i++;
}

